— PRIVACY POLICY —

To learn how the app is used and improve it, usage statistics are sent at most once a day. They are ANONYMOUS and NOT PERSONAL data: they can't tell who you are.

Only this is sent:
• a number chosen at random when the app is installed, not linked to your name, your account or any phone identifier;
• the phone's brand and model, the Android version, the app version and the language;
• how many days the app is used, how many times it's opened, how many songs are played and how many searches are made;
• how many minutes of music are played on the phone, in Android Auto, on a Chromecast and in video mode;
• whether a Google account is connected (yes or no, never which one), how many lists are on the phone and whether tastes were given.

NEVER sent: your name, email or Google account; your location; your phone number or phone identifiers; which songs, artists or searches you play or make; or the contents of your lists.

The data travels encrypted (HTTPS) and signed, and is kept in a private sheet of the app's owner, who only uses it to see overall statistics. It is never sold or shared with anyone.

Your tastes, history and lists stay on your phone. If you connect a Google account, the app talks directly to YouTube with that account, as the YouTube app would.
